Title: Worktree cleanup follows git's contract: ignored files and .tmp scratch are disposable
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-11-09T23:10Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context

Author decision, 2026-11-09, on the weekly ticket audit's recommendation
("your recommendations as is"). Two worktree-cleanup guards cost more than
they protect and are retired together, because they share six files.

**1. "Ignored files count as residue" (ticket 1212).** The rule exists
because the harness's own `.gitignore` is `*` with an allowlist. Every other
project ignores build products, caches and environments, which is what git
means by ignored, and pays for the harness's special case:

| Ticket | What the rule blocked | Patch it needed |
|---|---|---|
| 1406, 1458 | JETP's seeded data directory | byte-compare against `.worktreeinclude` (`worktree_setup_copy.py`) |
| 1487 | ignored build output in review copies, three projects in one day | `--ignored-ok`, allowed only on `review-*`/`gate-*` names |
| 1495 | uv venv internals (`.venv/.lock`) | allowlist of venv entries; three gaze FINDINGS rounds |

**2. The `.tmp` citation gate (ticket 1119).** Before a worktree's `.tmp/`
is deleted, `worktree-tmp-guard.py` lists forge requests, verdict files and
branch commits for a citation of `.tmp`, and fails closed when it cannot
look. It held about 9.8 GB in arena over an id type check (1470). The
audit's search of journal and tickets found no block for a real citation
(weak evidence: blocks are not logged). The rule that evidence lives outside
`.tmp/` already covers the case, and `.tmp/` is git-ignored by registration.

## Decision

- A git-ignored file is disposable in every worktree removal path (gaze,
  verify-gate, roar, lair, molt, gc): `git status --porcelain` without
  `--ignored` is the residue rule. Tracked changes, staged changes and
  untracked files that are not ignored still block, as do the lock, liveness
  and unpushed-commit rails, which this ticket does not touch.
- `.tmp/` is ignored scratch like any other: no citation search, no forge
  call, before removal. `worktree-tmp-guard.py register` (the `/.tmp/` line in
  `info/exclude`) stays; a size line before removal may stay if it costs
  nothing.
- Risk accepted by the author: in the harness, a file outside the allowlist
  (the root, or a new top-level directory) is ignored, so such a draft is
  deleted with its worktree. The allowlist un-ignores whole working
  directories (`scripts/**`, `skills/**`, `tests/**`, `tickets/**`,
  `design/**`, `rules/**`…), so drafts there stay visible as untracked.
  No replacement guard.

## Sites (origin/main, 2026-11-09; grep again before starting)

Residue rule: `scripts/worktree-clean-lib.sh` (`worktree_residue`,
`worktree_scrub`, `_venv_disposable`, `_build_child_*`),
`scripts/worktree_setup_copy.py` (delete), `scripts/worktree-exit-preflight.sh`
(`--ignored-ok` and its name check), `scripts/worktree-gc.sh`
(`ownerless_tree_clean`), `scripts/gaze_close.py`, `scripts/gate_tree.py`,
`skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md`, `skills/gaze/references/cleanup.md`,
`tests/test_preflight_ignored_ok.py`, `tests/test_worktree_tools.py`,
`tests/test_gaze_close.py`, `tests/test_roar_close_and_clean.sh`.

Citation gate: `scripts/worktree-tmp-guard.py` (`preflight` and `removal`
modes), its callers `scripts/gaze_close.py:145`,
`scripts/worktree-exit-preflight.sh:62`, `scripts/worktree-gc.sh:259`,
`skills/gaze/references/cleanup.md`, `skills/molt/SKILL.md`,
`skills/roar/references/close-and-clean.md`, `skills/lair/SKILL.md`, and
`tests/test_worktree_tools.py`, `tests/test_forge_status_scripts.py`,
`tests/test_review_panel_cleanup_contract.py`,
`tests/test_roar_close_and_clean.sh`.

`.worktreeinclude` itself is the runtime's file and is not removed from any
project; the harness only stops reading it for cleanup.

## Coordination

Ticket 1496's request (another session's coder) edits
`scripts/worktree-tmp-guard.py` and `skills/molt/SKILL.md`. Branch this
ticket only after that request has landed.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] An ignored file never blocks a worktree removal, in any project; a test shows one ignored file passing and one untracked, unignored file blocking, through the preflight and through gc
- [ ] `worktree_setup_copy.py`, `--ignored-ok` with its name check, the venv and build-output allowlists and their tests are deleted; no caller is left
- [ ] No removal path calls the forge or searches for `.tmp` citations; `worktree-tmp-guard.py` keeps `register`; a test shows a worktree whose `.tmp/` holds files being removed with no forge available
- [ ] Skill and reference text that restates either rule is brought in line; the two retirements are separate commits, so either can be reverted alone
- [ ] The request body states the lines removed and added, by area
- [ ] `make check` passes
